1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Big cops. Small town. Moderate violence.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Hot Fuzz is a crime, action, comedy film directed by Edgar Wright.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Former London constable Nicholas Angel finds it difficult to adapt to his
new assignment in the sleepy British village of Sandford.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Not only does he miss the excitement of the big city, but he
also has a well-meaning oaf for a partner.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
However, when a series of grisly accidents rocks Sandford, Angel
smells something rotten in the idyllic village.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Nicholas Angel, played by Simon Pegg.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
PC Danny Butterman, played by Nick Frost.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Inspector Frank Butterman, played by Jim Broadbent.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
DS Andy Wainwright, played by Paddy Considine.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
DC Andy Cartwright, played by Rafe Spall.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Sergeant Tony Fisher, played by Kevin Eldon.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Hot Fuzz is a 2007 British buddy cop action comedy film directed by
Edgar Wright, who co-wrote the film with Simon Pegg.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Pegg stars as Nicholas Angel, an elite London police officer, whose proficiency makes the rest of his team look bad,
causing him to be re-assigned to a West Country village where a series of gruesome deaths takes place.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Nick Frost stars alongside him as Police Constable
Danny Butterman, Angel's partner.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Hot Fuzz is the second and most commercially successful film in the Three Flavours
Cornetto trilogy, following Shaun of the Dead and followed by The World's End.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Over 100 action films were used as inspiration for the script.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
Principal photography took place in Wells, Somerset, for eleven weeks and ten artists
worked on VFX, which involved explosions, gory gunfire scenes and a flip book.

18
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
Released on 16 February 2007 in the United Kingdom and 20 April in the United States, Hot Fuzz received
acclaim from critics and grossed US$80 million worldwide on a budget of $12–16 million.

19
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
In 2020, Empire named it the 67th-greatest film of the 21st century.

20
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The film explores themes of countryside, police, village, arrest, parody.

21
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
The tone is lighthearted.
